1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19619, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019eQxSiCkfFziTNE6xaWu4T", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19619, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DAVYX3ARhyJTWBb3mwfv6o", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19919, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DAVYX3ARhyJTWBb3mwfv6o", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19919, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DAVYX3ARhyJTWBb3mwfv6o", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24612, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LJD6GnYx4oGynY6j1J6VhJ", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished, and all regions now run v2.3.0. After the rollback, the service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look into how v2.3.1 reached production after being unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55212, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LJD6GnYx4oGynY6j1J6VhJ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55212, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LJD6GnYx4oGynY6j1J6VhJ", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 56807, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CEch59sqMFrpbbyEFZRnf6", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57107, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CEch59sqMFrpbbyEFZRnf6", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57107, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CEch59sqMFrpbbyEFZRnf6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61810, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished. A status check confirmed us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had already been created as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), so I didn't resubmit and no duplicate page went out. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nINC-0001 also lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- Find out how v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01A3C5pdzTuEasoNQftUUDp5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01A6GBJURkc4K4dUZmkqE1cH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mrf9jrmdiwQixWEqQ3RAGw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017T2UFx2bxxwBPABTVSKoTE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XCeYa9LmJkhDm6SKQsgUYm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019eQxSiCkfFziTNE6xaWu4T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DAVYX3ARhyJTWBb3mwfv6o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LJD6GnYx4oGynY6j1J6VhJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished, and all regions now run v2.3.0. After the rollback, the service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and look into how v2.3.1 reached production after being unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CEch59sqMFrpbbyEFZRnf6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished. A status check confirmed us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had already been created as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), so I didn't resubmit and no duplicate page went out. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nINC-0001 also lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- Find out how v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}